However, some single-celled microorganisms, such as ciliates (Wood 1988a, b; Rajan et al. 2023) and amoebae (Boisseau et al. 2016), also exhibit habituation. Habituation to mechanical stimuli has been extensively demonstrated in ciliates (Dussutour 2021). For example, in the ciliate Stentor, the contraction response to mechanical stimulation is an example of habituation (Wood 1988a). In this habituation, changes in intracellular \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
