The spatial difference in the chemical decomposition rate contributes to the connection between the initial state shift and mitigation of deceleration. The relationship between the decomposition rates under stimulation in the front and rear parts determines the slope of the iso-acceleration line Eq. (21). In our simulation, \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
